# Structural merges (mergiraf) — syntax-aware merge driver for the languages
# agents edit concurrently (rebase/merge conflicts resolve at AST level, e.g.
# two agents appending to the same list/import block). Machines without the
# driver configured silently fall back to git's normal text merge. Setup:
#   brew install mergiraf   (or codeberg.org/mergiraf release binary)
#   git config --global merge.mergiraf.name mergiraf
#   git config --global merge.mergiraf.driver "mergiraf merge --git %O %A %B -s %S -x %X -y %Y -p %P -l %L"
*.go merge=mergiraf
go.mod merge=mergiraf
go.sum merge=mergiraf
*.kt merge=mergiraf
*.ts merge=mergiraf
*.tsx merge=mergiraf
*.json merge=mergiraf
*.yml merge=mergiraf
*.yaml merge=mergiraf
*.toml merge=mergiraf
# Lockfiles: resolve by regenerating, not merging — keep the default text
# driver so conflicts stay loud instead of getting auto-stitched.
andromeda/pnpm-lock.yaml -merge
